    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/46120": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Specialty Dental Medicine",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Specialty Dental Medicine Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Assistant Professor of Specialty Dental Medicine Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Specialty Dental Medicine Department Dental Clinic Position Category Faculty Job Description The Clinical Specialist plays a vital role in supporting patient care delivery, student clinical education, and the daily operations of the dental school clinic. This individual provides technical expertise in specialized areas of dentistry (e.g., prosthodontics, periodontics, oral surgery, endodontics), assists faculty in clinical instruction, ensures regulatory compliance, and helps maintain high standards of safety, efficiency, and patient service. The Clinical Specialist serves as a key resource for both students and clinical faculty Required Qualifications Dental degree (e.g., DDS , DMD ) with specialization or advanced training. Minimum of 3 years of clinical experience in a dental practice or academic setting preferred. Strong knowledge of specialty dental procedures, instrumentation, and materials. Excellent organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience working in an academic dental clinic. Familiarity with electronic health record systems (e.g., AxiUm). BLS certification and knowledge of emergency response protocols. Experience in mentoring or training dental students or staff Physical Demands Campus LMU Tower Job Duty Job Duty Clinical Support and Oversight: Provide expert support in designated specialty areas (e.g., removable prosthodontics, surgical setups, implant workflows). Prepare and maintain instruments, materials, and supplies needed for clinical procedures. Ensure treatment rooms and equipment are properly set up and maintained for optimal functionality. Job Duty Student Instruction and Guidance: Assist students during clinical sessions by reinforcing proper techniques and procedural protocols. Support faculty in evaluating students clinical performance and readiness for procedures.Promote professionalism, infection control, and patient-centered care among student providers Job Duty Specialty Clinic Operations: Coordinate specialty clinics and assist in managing appointment flow, faculty coverage, and case follow-up. Assist with documentation, case presentations, and interdepartmental referrals as needed Job Duty Quality Assurance and Compliance: Ensure adherence to clinic policies, infection control guidelines, HIPAA , and OSHA regulations. Participate in clinical audits, chart reviews, and safety checks. Report and assist in resolving clinical issues or patient concerns in a timely and professional manner Job Duty Training and Calibration: Participate in faculty and staff calibration sessions related to clinical protocols and evaluation criteria. Provide onboarding and continuing education support for new staff and students on specialty procedures and workflows Job Duty Inventory and Equipment Management: Monitor inventory levels of materials and supplies for assigned areas; assist in ordering and restocking. Ensure proper operation and maintenance of clinical and specialty equipment. Job Duty Interprofessional and Collaborative Support: Work closely with faculty, administrative teams, and dental assistants to support efficient and collaborative care. Serve as a liaison between clinical and academic departments when needed Job Duty Inclusive Excellence and Patient Experience: Contribute to a respectful, inclusive, and supportive clinic culture for all patients, students, and team members. Promote an environment that values cultural competence, empathy, and diversity in patient care Job Duty Other Duties as Assigned: Perform additional responsibilities as requested by clinic leadership in support of the institution s mission and clinical education objectives Posting Detail Information Posting Number F01842P Job Open Date 09/21/2026 Job Close Date 02/01/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/46101 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session 