    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/46135": {
      "title": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Principal Faculty, PA Program Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Principal Faculty, PA Program Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Principal Faculty, PA Program Department PA Program Knoxville Position Category Faculty Job Description The Physician Assistant Program clinical faculty shall have the responsibility of developing, executing, and monitoring clinical sites and preceptors, assuring compliance with SACS , ARCPA , and SMS policies and standards. The clinical faculty shall create and/or edit rotation-specific syllabi and preceptor evaluations of students. The clinical faculty shall be involved in teaching, evaluation and assessment, advisement, mentoring, and student compliance with LMU SMS policies. The clinical faculty shall participate in the recruitment, admissions and selection process, and program organization, evaluation, planning, administration, and management, and assist in continuous review and analysis of the LMU PA program curriculum effectiveness in preparation for program assessment by SACS , ARCPA , and SMS . Required Qualifications Graduation from an accredited physician assistant training program and certification by NCCPA ; current licensure or eligibility for Tennessee licensure; *possession of a masters degree in physician assistant studies and actively engaged or willing to obtain a doctoral degree in a field related to medical science; *minimum of two years full-time clinical experience as a physician assistant; *excellent oral, written, organizational, and computer skills. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in a field related to medical science or education; *teaching experience in classroom and clinical settings, preferably in an institution of higher learning; *program administrative or leadership experience; *evidence of potential for excellence in teaching and scholarly activity. Physical Demands Campus Job Duty Job Duty Promote the mission of Lincoln Memorial University to all faculty, staff, students, and to the community at large; Job Duty Promote effective working relationships among faculty, staff, and students; Job Duty Responsible for working with the Director of Clinical Education to identify and develop new clinical sites for PA clinical rotations and perform clinical site visits Job Duty Oversee qualitative and quantitative evaluations of students Job Duty Involved in program organization, evaluation, planning, administration and management as well as assist in continuous review and analysis of the program s effectiveness and preparation for program assessment by ARC -PA, LMU , SACSCOC , and others Job Duty Provide teaching, evaluation, advisement and mentoring of PA students Job Duty Work with LMU - SMS faculty and staff on an ongoing basis to maintain program compliance with the Accreditation Review Commission on Education for the Physician Assistant ( ARC -PA) and the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools ( SACS ) criteria for accreditation and reaccreditation; Job Duty Fulfill the University s scholarship expectation through research, publication, grant development, creative achievement, and other endeavors consistent with the Faculty/Staff Policy Manual; Job Duty Provide committee service and attend SMS , PA program and LMU faculty meetings Job Duty Develop course schedules, syllabi and student evaluation mechanisms; Job Duty Serve as Course Director for Clinical Phase courses as assigned and complete End-of-Course reports for assigned Clinical Phase courses and present conclusions based on data analysis and recommendations for action(s)/modification(s) to the Curriculum Committee. Job Duty Design, implement, coordinate, and evaluate learning and assessment activities for EOS days. Job Duty Assist in revising the Student Handbook and the Student Catalog as assigned. Job Duty Participate in the Program s continuous self-assessment process as directed. Job Duty Assist in recruiting, developing, evaluating, and maintaining clinical sites and clinical preceptors for Clinical Phase Supervised Clinical Practice Experiences (SCPEs). Job Duty Revise the Clinical Site/Preceptor Handbook with the assistance of the DCE and Clinical Site and Rotations Manager. Job Duty Develop, evaluate, and revise policies and procedures for the Clinical Phase with the DCE . Job Duty Participate in PA student selection; Job Duty Assure the availability of remedial instruction, as needed and assigned; Job Duty Participate in the design, implementation, coordination, and evaluation of PA program curriculum; *assist in the administration and evaluation of the PA program; Job Duty Assist in the search process for selecting PA program faculty; *establish a personal program of scholarly activity; Job Duty Write, edit, review, and approve learning objectives and test items; Job Duty Secure, orient, and evaluate clinical preceptors Job Duty Monitor student progress; serve as primary academic advisor for clinical year students; Job Duty Perform service activities that advance the PA program, SMS , and the PA profession, including assistance in the recruitment, orientation, and retention of PA students; as assigned; Job Duty Exhibit/recruit at various meetings as needed; *fulfill faculty responsibilities as outlined in the Faculty/Staff Policy Manual; Job Duty Complete required institutional, program accreditation, and other reports necessary for the advancement of University programs, both on campus and at extended campus sites; and perform other duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F01753P Job Open Date 09/23/2026 Job Close Date 03/31/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/44687 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Transcripts Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
