    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/46042": {
      "title": "Director of LMU Clinical DVM Program Operations & Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Director of LMU Clinical DVM Program Operations &amp; Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Director of LMU Clinical DVM Program Operations & Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Director of LMU Clinical DVM Program Operations & Assistant Professor Department CVM Clinical Relations Position Category Faculty Job Description The Director of LMU Clinical DVM Program Operations, in collaboration with the Executive Associate Dean of Clinical Relations and Outreach, and other Clinical Relations and Outreach faculty and staff, provides operational and executional expertise to the LMU Clinical DVM Program. The position will have input on shaping the LMU Clinical DVM program and educating future veterinarians. The position will be remote and will require occasional travel to LMU DVM instructional sites. Required Qualifications DVM Preferred Qualifications MBA or board certification; at least 10 years in clinical practice or academia Physical Demands Campus Remote Job Duty Job Duty Manage the LMU DVM Clinical Course Mentor Program Job Duty Manage the LMU DVM Clinical Site Training Program Job Duty Manage the LMU DVM Clinical Year Student Success Program Job Duty Manage the LMU DVM Professional Quality Assurance Program Job Duty Promote the mission of Lincoln Memorial University to all faculty, staff, students, and the community at large Job Duty Work closely and collaboratively with the Executive Associate Dean of Clinical Relations and Outreach. Job Duty Collaborate and foster working relationships with students, staff, peer faculty, other colleges on campus, and external partners 