    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45967": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy - Cardiopulmonary Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy - Cardiopulmonary Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy - Cardiopulmonary Department PHYSICAL THERAPY Position Category Faculty Job Description The Doctor of Physical Therapy Program at Lincoln Memorial University in Knoxville, Tennessee, invites applications for a full-time core faculty position at the Assistant Professor level. The successful candidate will contribute to the programs missions of teaching, scholarship, and service while joining a collaborative faculty dedicated to preparing the next generation of physical therapists. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a commitment to scholarly productivity, excellence in teaching, and professional service. Primary teaching responsibilities will focus on geriatric and cardiopulmonary physical therapy content within the graduate curriculum, with opportunities to contribute to additional areas consistent with the candidates expertise and program needs. Candidates with expertise in two or more of the following areas are particularly encouraged to apply: cardiopulmonary dysfunction and rehabilitation, acute care, wound care, pediatrics, and geriatrics. The anticipated start date is no later than July 1, 2027. Required Qualifications Doctorate in Physical Therapy degree ( DPT ) or BSPT / MSPT with academic doctorate Current licensure as a physical therapist in the state of Tennessee, or eligible to obtain licensure prior to initiating teaching duties Relevant clinical experience and expertise At least 3 years of clinical experience as a physical therapist Minimum of 2 years teaching experience in a clinical setting or at the college level Strong organizational skills and interpersonal skills Demonstrate the ability to foster a professional learning environment characterized by respect, fairness, collegiality, and support for student success. Strong commitment to student learning and success Ability to work independently, but demonstrated ability to collaborate within program faculty as well as with an interprofessional team Preferred Qualifications Academic doctorate (PhD, Ed.D. ScD, DHSc, etc.) in relevant field. ABD will be considered. Prior higher education teaching experience in a DPT program ABPTS Board Certified Specialist in relevant field Physical Demands Campus Lmu- West Knoxville Job Duty Job Duty Promote the mission of Lincoln Memorial University to all faculty, staff, students and to the community at large; Job Duty promote effective working relationships among faculty, staff and students; Job Duty contribute to the planning, development and evaluation of courses within the DPT program; Job Duty promote by precept and example a general atmosphere of respect for knowledge, thought and inquiry; Job Duty maintain intellectual integrity and to strive for academic excellence in teaching; Job Duty have on file in the appropriate office an outline and list of the goals and objectives for each lecture; Job Duty carry out lecture, seminar, small group discussion and/or clinical assignments and responsibilities effectively; Job Duty design and present a course, series of integrated lectures and/or small group discussions; Job Duty prepare examination questions as well as grade a course or portion of course; Job Duty meet classes according to published schedule; Job Duty serve as an active member of the program, working closely with the Program Director to further the Program, College, and University mission and vision; Job Duty serve as an example to learners and colleagues of appropriate professional behavior; Job Duty participate in scholarly activity; Job Duty serve as mentor to physical therapy and other healthcare profession students; Job Duty provide service by attending scheduled faculty meetings and by serving on appointed and or elected committees as required; Job Duty complete required institutional, program accreditation, and other reports necessary for the operation and advancement of the program; and Job Duty Demonstrate the ability to work effectively and professionally with students, colleagues, patients, and community partners from a broad range of backgrounds and perspectives Job Duty perform other duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F01828P Job Open Date 08/27/2026 Job Close Date 11/27/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45841 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
