    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45366": {
      "title": "Veterinary Assistant, Small Animal; OPCVM",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Veterinary Assistant, Small Animal; OPCVM Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Veterinary Assistant, Small Animal; OPCVM Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Veterinary Assistant, Small Animal; OPCVM Department CVM Clinical Sciences Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Veterinary Assistant for Small Animals supports the delivery of laboratory and clinical activities by assisting students, staff and faculty in assigned courses and educational tasks under licensed staff or faculty supervision. Responsibilities include organizing laboratories, generating schedules, managing training elements, collating supply requests, and coordinating with the site coordinator on facility needs. The Veterinary Assistant also ensures compliance with regulatory guidelines, manages records related to animals used in teaching, and provides hands-on assistance in teaching veterinary medical and surgical clinical skills. This position plays an essential role in preparing, setting up, cleaning, inventorying, and maintaining laboratory equipment and consumables to ensure a safe, efficient, and effective learning environment. Required Qualifications High school diploma Preferred Qualifications Associates degree or higher in a veterinary or animal-related field Knowledge of university program goals and objectives Experience in the veterinary medical field Training in animal care, handling, or husbandry Relevant experience in higher education Physical Demands Campus Orange Park Florida Job Duty Job Duty Assist designated staff and faculty in providing animal associated clinical and laboratory experiences for students in an efficient and professional manner Job Duty Support the education of students under faculty direction, helping them acquire veterinary medical and surgical clinical skills and entry-level competencies Job Duty Organize laboratories by preparing faculty, animals, student groups, equipment, and consumables Job Duty Assist with laboratory set-up, cleaning, inventorying, and replacement of equipment Job Duty Manage training elements and generate schedules for assigned activities Job Duty Maintain records and evaluations of students during clinical experiences Job Duty Assist with the handling, maintenance, monitoring, and care of small and large animals used in teaching Job Duty Ensure that all OSHA and USDA guidelines are implemented in student clinical activities Job Duty Assist with maintaining care of teaching animals in compliance with IACUC requirements including documentation in medical records Job Duty Ensure that all OSHA and USDA guidelines are implemented in student clinical activities Job Duty Oversee medical records of animals used in teaching and comply with IACUC requirements Job Duty Complete required institutional and program accreditation reports as well as other reports necessary for program advancement Job Duty Collate supply requests and ensure laboratory resources are available Job Duty Liaise with the site coordinator regarding facility requests and operational needs Job Duty Communicate directly with the Coordinator of Clinical Skills regarding human resource, animal, and operational matters Job Duty Foster effective working relationships among faculty, staff, and students Job Duty Promote the mission of Lincoln Memorial University to faculty, staff, students, and the community at large Job Duty Perform related duties in support of the College s and University s mission and evolving needs. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S05324P Job Open Date 06/01/2026 Job Close Date 09/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the