    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/46109": {
      "title": "Front Desk Coordinator, Dental, Knoxville",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Front Desk Coordinator, Dental, Knoxville Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Front Desk Coordinator, Dental, Knoxville Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Front Desk Coordinator, Dental, Knoxville Department Dental Clinic Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Front Desk Coordinator at the LMU Dental Clinic manages patient interactions and administrative tasks. Responsibilities include verifying patient financials and Medicaid status, processing check-ins and check-outs, and collecting fees from self-pay patients. The coordinator also assists with CareCredit financing, maintains accurate financial records, and updates patient accounts with a focus on posting and accuracy in EHR software. This role requires effective communication with dental staff and students, strong teamwork, and excellent customer service skills. Proficiency in Electronic Health Record management is essential. Top priorities include ensuring compliance with privacy regulations and maintaining accurate patient records. Required Qualifications .High school diploma or equivalent. .2 years experience in a medical or dental office setting. .This position is sedentary, requiring extended periods of sitting with occasional walking and standing. .Tasks may involve lifting no more than 25 pounds and occasionally carrying items like files or office supplies. .Able to multitask and prioritize tasks in a fast-paced environment Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Campus LMU Tower Job Duty Job Duty . Greet patients as they arrive and provide a welcoming environment Job Duty . Assist patients in filling out forms and obtaining necessary signatures Job Duty . Answer phones and schedule patients for dental screenings or treatment, addressing patient questions and concerns both in person and over the phone. Job Duty . Confirm patient financials before treatment is rendered; uphold clinic policy and procedures regarding payment at the time of service. Job Duty . Verify active Medicaid status on the day of the patient s appointment. Job Duty . Send and receive emails and faxes as needed to facilitate patient care and team communication Job Duty . Ensure all necessary patient documentation is completed and accurate, scan signed documents into patient electronic health record ( EHR ) software profile Job Duty . Process patient check-ins and check-outs efficiently and accurately using EHR software Job Duty . Assist patients with CareCredit financing. Reconcile end-of-day collection reports with credit card receipts and petty cash. Job Duty . Print student documents and patient forms as needed Job Duty . Keep the reception area clean and organized; order office supplies as needed Job Duty . Communicate with dental staff and students about patient arrivals and specific needs Job Duty . Assist with monitoring student attendance Job Duty . Collaborate with co-workers on patient scheduling, security processes, and patient management needs in the dental school setting Job Duty . Display a keen ability to multi-task, being a self-starter who consistently takes the initiative Job Duty . Ensure front office compliance with all CDC infection control, OSHA , HIPAA and state/federal debt collection regulations Job Duty . Actively participate in emergency protocols for codes and drills (medical, security, fire, weather, safety, etc.) Maintain BLS CPR healthcare certification Posting Detail Information Posting Number S04894P Job Open Date 12/17/2025 Job Close Date 12/31/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/42343 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
