    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45199": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Biostatistics",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Assistant/Associate Professor of Biostatistics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Assistant/Associate Professor of Biostatistics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Biostatistics Department Center for Animal Health/CAHA Position Category Faculty Job Description The faculty member in Biostatistics will provide primary consultative support to research-active faculty across the College, including study design, statistical methodology selection, data management planning, and advanced quantitative analysis for College-supported scholarly projects. The position will collaborate closely with investigators from project conception through dissemination, contributing to protocol development, statistical analyses, regulatory documentation, and preparation of peer-reviewed manuscripts. A limited teaching responsibility will include delivery of selected curriculum or workshops in biostatistics and research methods within the professional and/or graduate curriculum, consistent with departmental needs. Required Qualifications PhD in related field Preferred Qualifications DVM or equivalent Physical Demands Campus Harrogate Job Duty Job Duty Provide biostatistical consultation and methodological support to faculty across the College, including study design, data analysis, interpretation, and dissemination of scholarly work Job Duty Collaborate with investigators on research development activities, including grant preparation, protocol development, and manuscript preparation Job Duty Apply appropriate quantitative and statistical methods to a range of biomedical, clinical, and educational research questions Job Duty Support graduate students and faculty in statistical research design and analysis to advance high-quality scholarly inquiry Job Duty Deliver limited instructional content in biostatistics and research methodology within professional and/or graduate curricula, as assigned Job Duty Promote effective working relationships among faculty, staff, and students across departments and programs Job Duty Interact with academic leadership to coordinate research and instructional activities consistent with College and University priorities Job Duty Uphold ethical principles in research design, analysis, interpretation, and reporting Job Duty Participate in University and College committees and shared governance processes Job Duty Complete required institutional and program accreditation reports and other documentation necessary for academic operations Job Duty Perform other duties as assigned Posting Detail Information Posting Number F01680P Job Open Date 07/06/2026 Job Close Date 12/31/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background