    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/41806": {
      "title": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Patient Care Educator, Knoxville Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Patient Care Educator, Knoxville Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Patient Care Educator, Knoxville Department AHA Training Center Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Patient Care Educator for the DeBusk College of Osteopathic Medicine at Lincoln Memorial University-Knoxville ( DCOM at LMU -Knoxville) is responsible for providing learning support and instruction for osteopathic medical students in the areas of clinical and interpersonal skills, teamwork, communications, etc. through simulation and formative/summative evaluation. Required Qualifications Nursing ( LPN , RN or BSN ) , certified military medic (E4 or above), paramedic or related experience (at least 3 years). Preferred Qualifications Recent experience as an educator or skills instructor; *knowledge and expertise in medical surgical; *experience with life support and other clinical skills training; *experience with simulation as an educational tool or with hi-fidelity simulation manikins preferred but not required. Physical Demands Campus Lmu- West Knoxville Job Duty Job Duty promote the mission of Lincoln Memorial University to all faculty, staff, students, and to the community at large; Job Duty promote effective working relationships among faculty, staff, and students Job Duty communicate professionally and effectively with course directors, faculty and students Job Duty work with faculty on case development and rubrics for clinical encounters Job Duty Create rubrics using the clinical evaluation software (B-Line ) Job Duty train Standardized Participants (SPs) on cases and interpersonal skills feedback Job Duty assist with physical examination labs as needed Job Duty monitor student performance on (SP) encounters Job Duty learn and utilize simulation technology for teaching and assessing health professions students Job Duty provide faculty development with the use of simulation Job Duty assist with case/scenario writing if needed Job Duty assist with daily administrative operation of the simulation lab Job Duty support the operation of simulation manikins and instruct during activities Job Duty assist with clinical skills procedures training Job Duty organize and participate in community outreach programs Job Duty willing to acquire certification and serve as an BLS , ACLS , PALS instructor as appropriate Job Duty work within state and federal codes, statutes and regulations that govern Tennessee Job Duty participate on university committees Job Duty complete required institutional, program accreditation, and other reports necessary for the advancement of University programs, both on campus and at extended campus sites Job Duty perform other duties as assigned Posting Detail Information Posting Number S04261P Job Open Date 08/01/2025 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/38839 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Letter of Recommendation 1 Optional Documents Transcripts 2 Transcripts 3 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
