      "title": "Student Services Coordinator, Knoxville",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Student Services Coordinator, Knoxville Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Student Services Coordinator, Knoxville Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Student Services Coordinator, Knoxville Department DCOM STUDENT SERVICES Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Student Services Coordinator for LMU - DCOM will support the Assistant Dean of Students and Associate Dean of Students in coordinating student support and activities for the Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO) program. Required Qualifications bachelors degree. Preferred Qualifications prior student services experience Physical Demands Campus Job Duty Job Duty promote the mission of Lincoln Memorial University to all faculty, staff, students and to the community at large Job Duty promote effective working relationships among faculty, staff, students and community members Job Duty track student services accreditation requirements and manage strategic planning documents Job Duty develop, implement, and supervise special student events, such White Coat, Graduation, and awards ceremonies Job Duty assist with tracking and documentation of graduation requirements Job Duty conduct administrative tasks, travel requests, and budget management of student funds Job Duty collaborate with the Public Relations department to ensure correct branding and logos are used for external events Job Duty collaborate with Career Services, Alumni Services, and LMU facilities to coordinate student events Job Duty recruit, train, and supervise all DCOM student ambassadors and requests for student ambassador participation Job Duty accompany students on DCOM sponsored off-campus student trips including DO Day on the Hill (Washington, DC) and relevant DCOM sponsored trips Job Duty act as liaison between students and student services department Job Duty assist in the maintenance of student documents and records Job Duty perform other duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S05368P Job Open Date 07/14/2026 Job Close Date 11/14/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45260 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Transcripts 2 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
