    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/46113": {
      "title": "Director of Clinical Operations",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Director of Clinical Operations Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Director of Clinical Operations Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Director of Clinical Operations Department Dental Clinic Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Director of Clinical Operations is responsible for the leadership, management, and performance of all clinical operations within the Dental School. This position focuses exclusively on patient care delivery, clinic workflow efficiency, regulatory compliance, and operational support of the clinical education program. The Director ensures that clinic operations support student learning, faculty supervision, and high-quality patient care while maintaining financial sustainability within the clinical enterprise Required Qualifications Bachelors degree in Healthcare Administration, Business Administration, Public Health, or related field (Masters preferred). 5-8 years of progressive healthcare or dental clinic management experience. Strong understanding of dental clinic operations and revenue cycle management. Knowledge of healthcare regulatory requirements. Preferred Qualifications Experience in an academic dental school setting. Familiarity with dental practice management systems and EHR platforms. Experience managing multi-specialty or high-volume clinics. Physical Demands Campus LMU Tower Job Duty Job Duty Oversee daily operations of predoctoral and specialty dental clinics Job Duty Ensure efficient patient scheduling, chair utilization, and provider productivity Job Duty Monitor clinic performance metrics, including patient volume, treatment completion, and revenue Job Duty Implement policies and procedures to optimize workflow and service delivery Job Duty Maintain operational readiness of clinic spaces Job Duty Collaborate with academic leadership to ensure students meet clinical competency requirements. Job Duty Support faculty in delivering high-quality clinical instruction. Job Duty Assist in clinic calibration, standardization, and evaluation processes Job Duty Balance educational mission with operational performance goals Job Duty Monitor clinical revenue cycle performance, including billing, collections, and insurance processing Job Duty Work with finance teams on clinic budget management and forecasting Job Duty Identify opportunities to improve clinic efficiency and financial sustainability Job Duty Track key performance indicators (KPIs) and productivity benchmarks Job Duty Ensure compliance with OSHA , HIPAA , infection control standards, and state dental regulations. Job Duty Support accreditation processes (e.g., CODA ). Job Duty Oversee quality assurance and patient safety initiatives. Job Duty Address clinical incident reporting and risk mitigation Job Duty Supervise clinic managers, front desk teams, and clinical support staff. Job Duty Oversee hiring, onboarding, training, and performance evaluations. Job Duty Promote a culture of accountability, service excellence, and professionalism Job Duty Establish and maintain high standards for patient care and service Job Duty Address escalated patient concerns Job Duty Monitor patient satisfaction metrics Job Duty Other Duties as assigned Posting Detail Information Posting Number S05479P Job Open Date 09/21/2026 Job Close Date 01/21/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities,