    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45406": {
      "title": "Faculty Services Librarian and Assistant Professor of Law",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Faculty Services Librarian and Assistant Professor of Law Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Faculty Services Librarian and Assistant Professor of Law Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Faculty Services Librarian and Assistant Professor of Law Department Part-Time Law Program Position Category Faculty Job Description Under the general supervision of the Associate Director of the Law Library, the Faculty Services Librarian oversees research assistants, specialized research, and instructional and scholarly support services to law faculty. This position plays a central role in advancing faculty teaching resources and scholarship by delivering research assistance, providing training on instructional resources, and supporting the integration of legal research into the curriculum. The Faculty Services Librarian holds a non-tenure-track faculty appointment and will teach various legal research courses and potentially other courses within the law school curriculum Required Qualifications J.D. degree from an ABA -approved law school and experience in an academic law library; Master of Library and Information Science degree from an ALA -accredited program, or significant graduate-level coursework toward such a degree Preferred Qualifications Law library reference desk, help desk, or other customer service experience; familiarity with law library operations; familiarity with bibliographic classification systems, such as MARC , LC classification, or LCSH ; teaching, training, or other instruction experience; experience using technology for teaching or presenting to large groups; active law license; law practice experience. Physical Demands Campus Duncan School of Law Job Duty Job Duty provide sophisticated research and reference assistance to DSOL faculty Job Duty provide legal research instruction to DSOL students and faculty via workshops and guest lectures Job Duty provide research assistance to DSOL faculty and their research assistants Job Duty teach for-credit courses in the law school curriculum, including, but not limited to, Legal Research Job Duty serve as the liaison to the faculty to develop programming and provide services Job Duty develop instructional and scholarship assistance to faculty Job Duty oversee research assistants Job Duty support current awareness and emerging technologies Job Duty contribute to the Law Library s strategic initiatives Job Duty participate in the planning and implementation of new Law Library programs and procedures Job Duty serve on faculty committees as appointed by the Dean Job Duty attend faculty meetings other mandatory events for faculty Job Duty participate in the DSOL community by attending events and providing support to student activities Job Duty meet all other requirements of the faculty as set forth in the DSOL Appendix to the LMU Employee Handbook Job Duty other duties as assigned Posting Detail Information Posting Number F01814P Job Open Date 07/01/2026 Job Close Date 11/01/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, dis