      "title": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Manager of Student Events and Engagement Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Manager of Student Events and Engagement Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Manager of Student Events and Engagement Department DCOM CLINICAL MEDICINE Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Manager of Student Events and Engagement provides operational leadership for the planning, coordination, and execution of major student events and engagement initiatives across all LMU - DCOM campuses. Reporting to the Senior Associate Dean of Student Affairs, this position supervises the Student Life staff and ensures a consistent, high-quality student experience through the successful delivery of Orientation, White Coat Ceremony, Hooding and Awards Ceremony, Commencement, the Spring Formal, Match Day, and other institutional events. The Manager also supports Student Life initiatives as needed while promoting a vibrant and engaging student experience. Required Qualifications · Bachelor’s degree required. · Experience in event management, higher education, student affairs, hospitality, or a related field. · Excellent organizational, project management, communication, and budgeting skills. · Ability to manage multiple complex projects simultaneously. Preferred Qualifications · Experience in higher education or medical education. · Experience supervising staff and coordinating volunteers. · Experience with event management software, marketing platforms, and budget management. Physical Demands Campus Lmu- West Knoxville Job Duty Job Duty · Plan, coordinate, facilitate, and execute Orientation, White Coat Ceremony, Hooding and Awards C