    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45434": {
      "title": "Model and Inventory Assistant; OPCVM",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Model and Inventory Assistant; OPCVM Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Model and Inventory Assistant; OPCVM Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Model and Inventory Assistant; OPCVM Department CVM Clinical Sciences Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Model and Inventory Assistant supports the clinical skills curriculum by collaborating with the Coordinator of Clinical Skills to design, build, and maintain high-quality teaching models. This position ensures that models are functional, durable, and aligned with curricular objectives while assisting with laboratory preparation. Management of OPCVM inventory in conjunction with the Operations Section. The role requires creativity, technical proficiency, and the ability to collaborate with faculty, staff, and students to enhance veterinary education and maintain effective resource management Required Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Valid and current driver’s license Additional Requirements: The offer of employment is contingent upon the candidate meeting all University driver eligibility requirements. This position may require occasional overnight travel for program-related activities. Preferred Qualifications Experience in silicone-based molding, woodworking, construction, or model-building Knowledge of university program goals and objectives Familiarity with the veterinary medical field Relevant experience in higher education Physical Demands Campus Orange Park Florida Job Duty Job Duty Assist the Coordinator of Clinical Skills, in consultation with faculty, in designing and constructing clinical skills teaching models. Job Duty Create models and related learning materials to enhance student learning in alignment with curricular goals Job Duty Monitor the condition of existing models, performing routine maintenance, repairs, or replacements as needed Job Duty Innovatively solve model-related challenges related to durability, tactile properties, and functionality Job Duty Maintain accurate documentation of the model construction process and specifications Job Duty Work in support of the main campus CIVET workshop and the Director of CVM Model Building at the Harrogate, TN campus Job Duty Assist with setup and breakdown of clinical skills laboratories, ensuring models, equipment, and consumables are available. Job Duty Support veterinary technicians and faculty during laboratory sessions as needed Job Duty Maintain a safe, clean, and organized work and laboratory environment Job Duty Maintain accurate records of teaching models, tools, and supply inventory Job Duty Track usage and forecast needs to ensure adequate availability of resources Job Duty Coordinate ordering, receiving, storage, and distribution of supplies Job Duty Work collaboratively with faculty on interdisciplinary projects involving clinical skills models Job Duty Supervise veterinary student research assistants contributing to model development or inventory management Job Duty Participate in departmental, College, and University committees and initiatives. Job Duty Engage in community outreach and educational programs related to veterinary medicine and animal health Job Duty Foster effective working relationships among faculty, staff, and students Job Duty Maintain professionalism and courtesy in all interactions Job Duty Perform related duties in support of the College’s and University’s mission and evolving needs Posting Detail Information Posting Number S05008P Job Open Date 06/02/2026 Job Close Date 11/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/43168 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Transcripts To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
