      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Administrative Assistant for Student Affairs Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Administrative Assistant for Student Affairs Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Administrative Assistant for Student Affairs Department Academic & Student Support Ser Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Administrative Assistant for Student affairs will work closely with the Dean of Students as well as the student affairs leadership team and is responsible for general office operations and clerical support. Required Qualifications High School diploma required; AND Two years office experience and/or some formal post-high school coursework/clerical training. Preferred Qualifications Associate OR Bachelor degree. Physical Demands Campus Harrogate Job Duty Job Duty Track and process budgets, expenses, and financial reports for the Student Affairs department. Job Duty Assist with financial planning for events, programs, and departmental initiatives. Job Duty Process invoices and reimbursements, ensuring compliance with university policies. Job Duty Take detailed minutes during meetings and distribute them to relevant staff. Job Duty Coordinate follow-up actions and ensure that tasks are completed on time. Job Duty Coordinate and schedule appointments, meetings, and events for the Student Affairs staff. Job Duty Manage calendars, including room reservations and participant availability. Job Duty Ensure timely communication of meeting details and logistical support. Job Duty Respond to emails, phone calls, and other inquiries in a professional manner. Job Duty Assist with the creation and dissemination of departmental 