    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45796": {
      "title": "Student Activities Coordinator, DCOM, Harrogate",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Student Activities Coordinator, DCOM, Harrogate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Student Activities Coordinator, DCOM, Harrogate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Student Activities Coordinator, DCOM, Harrogate Department DCOM STUDENT SERVICES Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Student Activities Coordinator for DCOM will develop and implement all student activities, coordinate community outreach programs and large scale events, and assist in the oversight of student clubs and organizations. Required Qualifications *high school diploma. Preferred Qualifications *bachelors degree; prior student services experience. Physical Demands Campus Harrogate Job Duty Job Duty . Promote the mission of Lincoln Memorial University to all faculty, staff, students and to the community at large. Job Duty . Promote effective working relationships among faculty, staff, students, and community members. Job Duty . Participate on university committees. Job Duty . Act as liaison between students and student services department. Job Duty . Assist with the implementation of large-scale events and special projects, including Orientation, College Olympics, Fall Fest, Holiday Dinners, Gala, White Coat Ceremony, Donor Memorial Service, Award and Induction Ceremonies, and Graduation. Job Duty . Schedule all major events with the PR office, building coordinators, campus security and risk management. Job Duty . Create and maintain student activities calendar. Job Duty . Implement weekly programming for students, including social activities, wellness and fitness activities, and club meetings. Job Duty . Approve student activities requests working closely with Student Services staff members and decide which student activities are appropriate. Job Duty . Submit appropriate student activities requests to LMU s event approval committee. Job Duty . Support community outreach programs. Job Duty . Recruit and supervise community volunteer opportunities for students and student groups. Job Duty . Coordinate summer camps for high school and college programs. Job Duty . Assist with the development and implementation of wellness activities and initiatives, including DCOM Strong, DCOM Adventure Series, fitness programs, and intramural sports programs. Job Duty . Market and advertise events to DCOM community. Job Duty . Oversee DCOM Student Life social media accounts. Job Duty . Collaborate with public relations (PR) department to ensure correct branding and logos are used for external events and fundraising merchandise. Job Duty . Accompany students on DCOM sponsored off-campus student trips, including DO Day on the Hill (Washington, DC), AOA conference, ski trip, and other DCOM sponsored trips. Job Duty . Collaborate with Student Services and Admissions for college assignments and orientation activities. Job Duty . Perform other duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S05452P Job Open Date 08/24/2026 Job Close Date 12/31/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45795 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Transcripts 2 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
