    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45284": {
      "title": "Associate Admissions Coordinator, PA Program",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Associate Admissions Coordinator, PA Program Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Associate Admissions Coordinator, PA Program Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Associate Admissions Coordinator, PA Program Department PA Program Harrogate Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Associate Admissions Coordinator for the LMU / DCOM Physician Assistant (PA) Program is responsible for assisting in the advising of prospective applicants for admission to the PA Program, coordinating/processing and maintaining the applicant files, and maintaining student health and immunization records, and other duties pertaining to student admissions and advancement as assigned. There may be infrequent short-term travel associated with the position that may require overnight stays for purposes of recruiting. Occasional participation in activities of the PA program that occur after normal work hours to include weekends. Position requires frequent interaction with the public to include applicants and others seeking information on our program so strong presentation and verbal skills required. Computer skills required include working knowledge of MS Word, Excel and PowerPoint. Working knowledge of database data entry and maintenance will be expected and LMU Harrogate database specific training will be provided. Other activities for the program must be supported as defined by the admissions coordinator and program director. Required Qualifications Preferred Qualifications *experience in graduate or professional admissions processes. Physical Demands Campus Harrogate Job Duty Job Duty *promote the mission of Lincoln Memorial University to all faculty, staff, students and to the community at large; Job Duty *promote effective working relationships among faculty, staff and students; Job Duty *participate on university committees; Job Duty *assist in program planning and development; Job Duty *interpret, monitor and analyze information regarding operating policies and procedures; Job Duty *adhere to department budget; Job Duty *coordinate academic and/or staff personnel matters; Job Duty *provide assistance to resolution of problems that have a significant impact on the overall goals of the department; Job Duty *respond to telephone inquiries and e-mail inquiries regarding the admissions process; Job Duty *process application information, supplementary applications and supporting documentation; Job Duty *update applicant files and notify students of application status; Job Duty *assist with the planning and implementation of on-campus and off-campus events, orientation and commencement activities; Job Duty *schedule and conduct campus tours; Job Duty *assist with the recruitment plan for the LMU / DCOM PA Program; Job Duty *complete required institutional and program accreditation reports and other reports necessary for the operation and advancement of the University; Job Duty *perform other duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S05369P Job Open Date 07/16/2026 Job Close Date 11/16/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45283 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Curriculum Vitae To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45922": {
      "title": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Standardized Patient (SP) Educator, Knoxville Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Standardized Patient (SP) Educator, Knoxville Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Standardized Patient (SP) Educator, Knoxville Department Health Sciences Accreditation Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Standardized Patient (SP) Educator manages the recruitment, training, and operational delivery of human-simulation actors within the Clinical Exam Center at major campus hubs. This role ensures that live patient simulations are delivered with realistic accuracy and behavioral consistency. In a matrixed shared-services deployment model, this position functions under a dual-reporting framework. While reporting administratively to the centralized Director of Simulation and SP Programming, the SP Educator operates under the direct functional, day-to-day programmatic supervision of the local Program Director (or designated program faculty) during the planning, dry-running, and execution of program-specific curricular events to satisfy programmatic staff adequacy and autonomy standards (e.g., ARC -PA Standards A2.11 and A2.12). Required Qualifications Successful acquisition of the CHSOS or CHSE credential through the Society for Simulation in Healthcare within two years of hire required Preferred Qualifications Bachelors degree in education, theater, healthcare, communication, or related experience. Experience in instructional training, corporate coaching, acting instruction, or clinical skills education Experience working within an accredited health professions program framework preferred Physical Demands Campus Job Duty Job Duty SP Performance Training: Lead patient encounter case training, role-play modeling, and calibration sessions to ensure SPs portray medical scenarios accurately Job Duty Encounter Workflow Management: Direct the on-site flow of medical students and SPs through exam rooms during active clinical assessments Job Duty Personnel Pipeline Management: Execute local recruitment initiatives, conduct interviews/mock encounters, and run onboarding orientations for new SP actors Job Duty Administrative Administration: Manage local SP payroll logging, track local hours, and conduct ongoing quality assurance performance reviews for SP personnel Job Duty Case Setup: Organize physical paperwork, props, and digital checklists within exam rooms prior to live assessments Job Duty Academic Governance Compliance: Adhere strictly to the case guidelines, checklists, rubrics, and educational directives provided by the local Program Director or designated faculty, operating as an operational extension of the program s curricular design Job Duty Professional Development & Knowledge Sharing: Attend at least one national or regional conference per year related to core responsibilities to bring back innovative practices and knowledge to faculty and staff Job Duty Multi-Site Mobility: Travel between university locations and regional campuses as needed to meet the operational requirements of the job Job Duty Key Competencies Exceptional behavioral coaching and training skills. Logistics and human resource management. High interpersonal empathy and professionalism tracking. Local operational autonomy and adherence to strict regulatory/accreditation standards Job Duty Achieving a high standard of case portrayal accuracy and behavioral calibration across all local SP actors, preventing scoring variances due to actor inconsistency Job Duty Safe, timely, and organized student/actor traffic control through exam matrix rooms during complex, multi-station clinical assessments Job Duty Sustaining a diverse, highly trained local SP pipeline through continuous recruitment, leading to zero staffing shortages during high-volume exam weeks Job Duty 100% accuracy in tracking local hours, processing administrative paperwork, and submitting payroll records in line with institutional deadlines Job Duty Positive performance evaluations and feedback from the local Program Director(s) regarding adherence to program-specific protocols, operational execution, and behavioral calibration Job Duty Successful acquisition of the Certified Healthcare Simulation Operations Specialist ( CHSOS ) credential through the Society for Simulation in Healthcare within two years of hire, utilizing university-sponsored professional development resources Posting Detail Information Posting Number S05448P Job Open Date 08/17/2026 Job Close Date 12/17/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45728 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts Curriculum Vitae To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
