    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45453": {
      "title": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Clinical Relations Veterinarian Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Clinical Relations Veterinarian Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Clinical Relations Veterinarian Department CVM Clinical Relations Position Category Faculty Job Description The Clinical Relations Veterinarian, in collaboration with the Associate Dean for Clinical Relations and Outreach and other Clinical Relations and Outreach faculty and staff, provides strategic leadership and promotes excellence in all phases of clinical rotations for fourth year veterinary students. The Clinical Relations Veterinarian shall be in charge of liaising with Clinical Affiliates (Clinical Site Preceptors) involved in clinical year curriculum delivery. The Clinical Relations Veterinarian shall facilitate the training and professional development of Clinical Site Preceptors and their associated teams. The Clinical Relations Veterinarian will lead efforts to secure additional Clinical Affiliate partners and to represent the LMU - CVM at select professional meetings. The Clinical Relations Veterinarian will ensure excellence in student learning experiences during all clinical year rotations. The Clinical Relations Veterinarian will participate in delivering course content and teaching in the Clinical and Professional Skills course and other LMU - CVM pre-clinical courses. The Clinical Relations Veterinarian will have input on shaping the LMU - CVM program and the education of future veterinarians. The Clinical Relations Veterinarian will be assigned geographic regions and will be responsible for all aspects for program delivery in that area including Affiliate Recruiting, Affiliate Relationship Management, Student Support, Managing the Clinical Hub Liaisons that are in the area and problem solving relative to their area. Required Qualifications DVM / VMD degree, *a working knowledge of information systems and databases. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Campus Remote Job Duty Job Duty Promote the mission of Lincoln Memorial University to all faculty, staff, students and to the community at large Job Duty promote effective working relationships among faculty, staff and students Job Duty contributes to the overall success of the academic team and the university of the whole Job Duty collaborate and foster working relationships with peers, other colleges on campus, and external partners and stakeholders to attain the college s and university s goals and objectives Job Duty participate on University committees Job Duty undertake the Standard Instructional/Research/Service Workload as outlined in the LMU Faculty Staff Policy Manual Job Duty supervise the planning, delivery, and evaluation of designated courses Job Duty works closely and collaboratively with the Associate Dean of Clinical Relations and Outreach Job Duty provides oversight for implementation of initiatives and the strengthening of the fulfillment of the college mission Job Duty assures student learning outcomes are achieved and measurable in both qualitative and quantitative metrics in the hybrid distributed clinical education model Job Duty participate in regularly scheduled meetings of personnel assigned to the Clinical Relations and Outreach team Job Duty prepare required reports; *assures that the college is represented at appropriate AAVMC , AVMA , State VMAs and other professional programs, initiatives, and events as designated Job Duty ability to effectively deliver presentations to students, clinical affiliates and other parties Job Duty recruit new clinical affiliate partners into the LMU - CVM clinical affiliate network in designated geographic areas Job Duty recruit new clinical affiliate partners into the LMU - CVM clinical affiliate network in designated geographic as identified Job Duty ability to travel regularly Job Duty perform other duties as assigned Posting Detail Information Posting Number F01816P Job Open Date 07/31/2026 Job Close Date 11/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45452 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session