    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45359": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy - Neurologic Rehabilitation Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy - Neurologic Rehabilitation Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy - Neurologic Rehabilitation Department PHYSICAL THERAPY Position Category Faculty Job Description The Doctor of Physical Therapy Program at Lincoln Memorial University in Knoxville, Tennessee invites applications for a full-time core faculty position. The successful candidate will contribute to the programs missions of teaching, scholarship, and service while joining a collaborative faculty dedicated to preparing the next generation of physical therapists. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a commitment to scholarly productivity, excellence in teaching, and professional service. Primary teaching responsibilities will focus on neurologic physical therapy and neuromuscular rehabilitation content within the graduate curriculum, with opportunities to contribute to additional areas consistent with the candidates expertise and program needs. A Fall 2026 start date is preferred. Required Qualifications Doctorate in Physical Therapy degree ( DPT ) or BSPT / MSPT with academic doctorate; current licensure and a physical therapist in the state of Tennessee, or eligible to obtain licensure prior to initiating teaching duties; relevant clinical experience in neurological rehabilitation; at least 3 years of clinical experience as a physical therapist; minimum of 2 years teaching experience in a clinical setting or at the college level. Preferred Qualifications Academic doctorate (PhD, EdD, ScD, DHSc, etc.) in relevant field, ABD will be considered; ABPTS Board Certified Specialist in neurology ( NCS ) and/or pediatrics ( PCS ); additional related neurological certification/s (e.g., CSRS , CBIS , PWR ! Moves, vestibular certification, LSVT BIG and/or LOUD , CEEAA ); additional continuing education/certifications in relevant field; experience with the CAPTE accreditation process. Physical Demands Campus Job Duty Posting Detail Information Posting Number F01811P Job Open Date 07/21/2026 Job Close Date 10/21/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45306 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
