    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45982": {
      "title": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Encounters - Standardized Patients, Brandon, FL Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Encounters - Standardized Patients, Brandon, FL Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Encounters - Standardized Patients, Brandon, FL Department Health Sciences Simulations Position Category Staff Part Time Job Description Standardized Patients (SPs) at the Center for Interprofessional Education and Simulation ( CIPES ) across the Lincoln Memorial University ( LMU ) Health Sciences enterprise in Brandon, Florida, serve as an integral part of the healthcare education team. SPs accurately and consistently portray specific patient cases, behaviors, and physical findings to help medical, nursing, and other health profession students refine their clinical skills in a safe, simulated environment. This role is vital for ensuring high-quality, hands-on training that supports student academic success and optimal patient care across LMUs health sciences programs. This role reports directly to the Standardized Patient Educator for Florida campuses. Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED required; no higher education degree required. Acting or role-playing experience preferred, but not required. Strong verbal communication, memory, and interpersonal skills. Ability to read, memorize, and accurately replicate case details, physical symptoms, and behavioral cues. Comfortable undergoing non-invasive physical examinations by health professional students. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Campus LMU Tampa Job Duty Job Duty Accurately and consistently portray specific patient cases, roles, and scenarios following training and rehearsal Job Duty Simulate all aspects of a patient scenario, including medical history, emotional affect, behavior, and physical findings in a standardized and reliable manner Job Duty Prepare for assigned simulations by studying case materials and patient roles prior to student encounters. Job Duty Demonstrate and evaluate history-taking and interviewing skills with medical, nursing, and other health sciences learners Job Duty Complete checklists and performance evaluations of student interactions accurately, consistently, and objectively. Job Duty Accept and incorporate trainer and supervisor feedback to continuously refine case portrayals and assessment accuracy. Job Duty Maintain strict objectivity and confidentiality regarding student performance, cases, and simulation materials Job Duty Exhibit reliability, flexibility, and punctuality with scheduled training sessions, rehearsals, and simulation events Job Duty Interact professionally and collaboratively with learners, faculty, staff, and peer standardized patients Job Duty Promote the mission and values of Lincoln Memorial University to students, faculty, staff, and the broader community Job Duty Foster effective, positive working relationships across all LMU Health Sciences programs and departments. Job Duty Complete required institutional, program accreditation, and administrative reports necessary for university advancement Job Duty Perform other related duties as assigned Posting Detail Information Posting Number S05467P Job Open Date 09/03/2026 Job Close Date 12/03/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45972 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
