    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45370": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant for Clinical Sciences; OPCVM",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Administrative Assistant for Clinical Sciences; OPCVM Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Administrative Assistant for Clinical Sciences; OPCVM Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Administrative Assistant for Clinical Sciences; OPCVM Department CVM Clinical Sciences Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Administrative Assistant for Clinical Sciences is a full-time position responsible for providing administrative support to the Office of Clinical Sciences ( OCS ) and serving as the designated administrative assistant for the Associate Dean of Clinical Sciences. This role involves providing operational support, coordinating office activities, and assisting faculty and staff with various administrative tasks. The Administrative Assistant will collaborate to ensure the smooth functioning of the office and contribute to the mission of the University, the College of Veterinary Medicine at Orange Park and the Office of Clinical Sciences Required Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Preferred Qualifications Office setting experience Some college Knowledge of university program goals and objectives Familiarity with veterinary medical field Relevant experience in higher education Physical Demands Campus Job Duty Job Duty Manage daily office operations, including answering phones, responding to emails, and handling correspondence Job Duty Schedule and coordinate meetings, appointments, and events for the OCS Job Duty Maintain and organize office files, records, and databases Job Duty Assist with the preparation and submission of reports, grants, and other documents Job Duty Serve as the initial point of contact for the OCS , providing information and assistance to faculty, staff, students, and external partners Job Duty Facilitate communication between the OCS and other university offices and departments Job Duty Draft and edit correspondence, reports, and other documents as needed Job Duty Assist with budget monitoring, including tracking expenses, processing invoices and purchase cards Job Duty Coordinate office purchasing and inventory, ensuring supplies and equipment are adequately stocked Job Duty Assist with OCS and College events, such as Student Affairs events, seminars, workshops, and conferences Job Duty Assist with logistics for events, including venue booking, catering, and travel arrangements Job Duty Handle sensitive and confidential information with discretion in compliance with University procedures as well as state and federal regulations Job Duty Maintain professionalism and courtesy in all interactions and communications Job Duty Assist in community outreach and education programs related to veterinary medicine and animal health Job Duty Collaborate and foster working relationships with peers, other colleges on campus, and external partners and stakeholders to attain the College s and University s goals Job Duty Support the Operations section with administrative tasks as needed Job Duty Perform related duties in support of the College s and University s mission and evolving needs Posting Detail Information Posting Number S04956P Job Open Date 05/07/2026 Job Close Date 10/31/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/42794 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Transcripts To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
