      "title": "Director of the Library",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Director of the Library Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Director of the Library Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. \"Flexible or hybrid work arrangements may be considered based on the qualifications of the successful candidate, the responsibilities of the position, and the operational needs of the University.\" Position Details Position Information Position Title Director of the Library Department FINLEY LEARNING RESOURCE CNT Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Director of the Library shall be directly responsible for the operation of the Carnegie Vincent Library, including the Reed Medical and Allied Health Sciences Library and the Mabel Smith Music Library. Flexible or hybrid work arrangements may be considered based on the qualifications of the successful candidate, the responsibilities of the position, and the operational needs of the University. Required Qualifications MLS or MLIS from an ALA accredited program; at least three years administrative experience working in an academic library. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate in Library Science or related field Physical Demands Campus Harrogate Job Duty Job Duty Promote the mission of Lincoln Memorial University to all faculty, staff, students and to the community at large Job Duty Promote effective working relationships among faculty, staff, and students Job Duty chair the Library and Learning Resources Committee, serve on other University Job Duty committees as needed Job Duty administer the effective and efficient operation of all aspects of library service, including the health sciences library Job Duty develop and implement policies and procedures, in consultation with the Library and Learning Resources Committee, necessary for the operation and promotion of the library Job Duty coordinate, in consultation with the Library and Learning Resources Committee, the development of the library collection, maintain a collection responsive to the needs of the faculty, staff, and students Job Duty promote and maintain professional relationships with the faculty, staff, and students Job Duty promote the library Job Duty maintain the library s budget Job Duty oversee hiring of all library personnel; train, supervise and evaluate job performance of all direct reports and provide direction on personnel maters to unit supervisors. Job Duty participate in activities designed to enhance professional and scholarly development Job Duty complete required institutional, program accreditation and other reports necessary for the operation and advancement of University programs, both on campus and at extended campus sites Job Duty perform other duties as assigned Job Duty maintain strict confidentiality regarding library patron records and other University matters Posting Detail Information Posting Number S05459P Job Open Date 08/27/2026 Job Close Date 12/31/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary “Flexible or hybrid work arrangements may be considered based on the qualifications of the successful candidate, the responsibilities of the position, and the operational needs of the University.” About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45853 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
