      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Adjunct Faculty, Chattanooga Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Adjunct Faculty, Chattanooga Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Chattanooga Department Physician Assistant Program Chattanooga Position Category Adjunct Job Description The Adjunct Faculty member contributes to the Physician Assistant (PA) Program by delivering high-quality instruction in their area of subject matter expertise. Adjunct Faculty may be clinicians, researchers, educators, or professionals with specialized knowledge, hired to teach specific content during the didactic or clinical phase of the curriculum. This role is essential to maintaining academic rigor and supporting student success through well-prepared, relevant, and engaging instruction Required Qualifications Subject matter expertise relevant to the course being taught. Educational and/or professional background appropriate to instructional content (e.g., clinical experience, academic training, research experience, certifications). Prior teaching or instructional experience is preferred but not required. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Note: Qualifications will vary based on the instructional topic. Specific credentialing or licensing may be required for clinically related content. Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching or instructional experience is preferred but not required. Physical Demands Campus Chattanooga Job Duty Posting Detail Information Posting Number F01834P Job Open Date 09/07/2026 Job Close Date 09/01/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a 