    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/39950": {
      "title": "Lower Level Instructor, J Frank White Academy",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Lower Level Instructor, J Frank White Academy Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Lower Level Instructor, J Frank White Academy Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Lower Level Instructor, J Frank White Academy Department JFWA Position Category Faculty Job Description The primary responsibility of the instructional faculty member is to teach assigned courses in accordance with the mission and standards of the J. Frank White Academy. *Currently filling a position and seeking an individual qualified in teaching language(s), Spanish preferred, but qualified applicants in French, German, and/or Latin will be considered. Required Qualifications Elementary certification required; degree in subject area taught as well as 12 hours of professional education courses and six hours of coursework every five years taught; and *Tennessee certification in area of specialization or appropriate permit/interim license. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Campus Harrogate Job Duty Job Duty promote the mission of the J. Frank White Academy and Lincoln Memorial University to all faculty, staff, students and to the community at large Job Duty *promote effective working relationships among faculty, staff and students Job Duty participate on University committees Job Duty teach classes assigned by the Principal Job Duty develop and distribute a course syllabus for each class assigned, and present copies to students, parents and the Principal Job Duty teach each class within the framework of the mission of the Academy, the University, and the syllabus as presented Job Duty establish course objectives for each course taught and create lesson plans aligned with Tennessee standards for the grade and content area taught Job Duty assist in revision of curriculum as assigned Job Duty evaluate enrolled students and submit grades in a timely fashion Job Duty requisition materials required Job Duty participate in the evaluation process and utilize the results to improve teaching effectiveness Job Duty participate in events that support the institution, the faculty, staff and students Job Duty assist at Academy basketball games, parent nights, open houses, preview nights, commencement, fundraisers and other duties as assigned Job Duty advise one Academy organization Job Duty update knowledge and skills Job Duty leave materials/plans for substitute teachers Job Duty maintain compliance with Southern Association of Colleges and Schools/AdvancED requirements for faculty members Job Duty comply with the Academy Faculty Handbook and the LMU Employee Handbook Job Duty provide 180 days of instruction plus five full days of in-service Job Duty *attend monthly faculty meetings Job Duty participate on faculty committees as assigned Job Duty *sponsor at least one student organization (including after school or evening work associated with this sponsorship) Job Duty work athletic events and open house events during the year Job Duty perform other duties as assigned Job Duty complete required institutional and program accreditation reports and other reports necessary for the operation and advancement of the University and the J. Frank White Academy. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F01473P Job Open Date 05/19/2025 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-8