    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/46110": {
      "title": "Scheduling Coordinator",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Scheduling Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Scheduling Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Scheduling Coordinator Department Dental Clinic Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description As a Scheduling Coordinator, you are responsible for scheduling patient appointments, handling phone calls, and ensuring accurate data entry in the Electronic Health Record ( EHR ) system. Key tasks include explaining treatments to patients, scheduling and confirming appointments, and maintaining accurate treatment plans and appointment data. The Scheduling Coordinator optimizes daily, weekly, and monthly patient schedules, discusses financial arrangements, and presents financing options. Knowledge and compliance with CDC , HIPAA , OSHA , and other regulations is essential. Your ability to communicate effectively is crucial for collaborating with the clinic team to meet the needs of both students and patients Required Qualifications 2 years dental office experience, or comparable healthcare or financial administration experience. High school diploma or equivalent. Must be able to lift up to 25 pounds and spend long periods of time standing or sitting Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Campus Morristown Job Duty Job Duty This position requires a working knowledge of dentistry to assist the Faculty Team Leader, student dentist and clinic faculty and staff in explaining treatments to patients Job Duty Responsible for scheduling DMD student patient appointments. Facilitate patient check-in and check-out with front desk team and building security staff Job Duty Handle incoming phone calls to schedule appointments, take messages for students and clinic staff and answer questions as needed. Use phone scripts provided for new patient, emergency or appointment cancellation calls Job Duty Become proficient in using clinic EHR software. Job Duty Oversee the patient schedule to ensure efficient daily, weekly, and monthly schedule and chair utilization, following clinic scheduling guidelines Job Duty Maintain and monitor the accuracy of EHR data, including treatment plan and appointment data entered by students Job Duty Efficiently track daily, weekly, and monthly progress on group/student production/collection goals to maintain productive clinic operations Job Duty Present a warm, confident, compassionate, and professional appearance and demeanor, whether on the phone or in person. Exemplify a caring attitude, cheerfulness, and eagerness to help. Job Duty Communicate directly with patients; confirm patient appointments for the next day and monitor text and email communication systems periodically throughout the day Job Duty Speak with patients regarding financial arrangements; ensure that all patients seen have a signed treatment plan with firm financial arrangements in their EHR before scheduling the next appointment. Seek guidance from the Clinic Manager or Patient Care Coordinator if a patient is unable to pay. Job Duty Assist patients with outgoing referrals to specialists or medical professionals for treatment or consultation; coordinate care with the patient s student dentist/Faculty Lead. Job Duty Complete CareCredit training and be prepared to present financing information to patients Job Duty Regularly monitor open treatment per student, including past due recall, in conjunction with the Clinical Supervisor and Faculty Lead to maintain student competencies Job Duty Display a keen ability to multi-task, be a self-starter and consistently take the initiative Job Duty Ensure practice compliance with all CDC , HIPAA , OSHA and Fair Debt Collection Practices Act guidelines and regulations Job Duty Follow practice protocols for patient financial arrangements and seek assistance from supervisors as needed Job Duty Respond to patient inquiries to ensure patient satisfaction Job Duty Collaborate with front office and clinical team to ensure student and patient requirements are met Job Duty Review management reports to improve schedule performance Job Duty Assist with tracking student attendance. Job Duty Actively participate in emergency protocols for codes and drills (medical, security, fire, weather, safety, etc. Job Duty Perform other duties as assigned Posting Detail Information Posting Number S05272P Job Open Date 05/07/2026 Job Close Date 10/31/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/44137 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation 1 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
