    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/46112": {
      "title": "Associate Dean for Faculty and Students",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Associate Dean for Faculty and Students Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Associate Dean for Faculty and Students Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Associate Dean for Faculty and Students Department College of Dental Medicine Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Dean of Students and Faculty in a dental school plays a pivotal role in shaping the educational experience of future dental professionals, ensuring academic excellence, and fostering a supportive and innovative environment for faculty and students alike Required Qualifications A doctoral degree in dentistry (D.D.S. or D.M.D) preferred .Extensive experience in academic leadership, preferably within a dental school or similar healthcare educational institution. Strong understanding of accreditation standards, educational trends, and regulatory requirements in dental education. Excellent communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills. Visionary leadership with a commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion in education and practice. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Campus LMU Tower Job Duty Job Duty Curriculum Development: Collaborate with faculty members to design and update the dental curriculum, ensuring it meets accreditation standards and prepares students for professional practice. Job Duty Educational Policies: Develop and enforce policies related to academic standards, student progression, and assessment procedures Job Duty Quality Assurance: Monitor the quality of teaching and learning within the dental school, promoting continuous improvement and innovation in educational methods Job Duty Faculty Recruitment: Participate in the selection and hiring of faculty members, ensuring a diverse and qualified teaching staff Job Duty Professional Development: Support faculty development through workshops, seminars, and opportunities for research and publicatio Job Duty Performance Evaluation: Conduct regular evaluations of faculty performance, providing feedback and support for career advancement Job Duty Student Services: Oversee student services such as counseling, career advising, and academic support to promote student well-being and success Job Duty Student Discipline: Address student conduct issues in accordance with school policies, promoting a positive and respectful learning environment Job Duty Student Engagement: Foster a sense of community and engagement among students through extracurricular activities, clubs, and events Job Duty Budget Management: Develop and manage the budget for the dental school, allocating resources effectively to support academic and administrative needs if assigned. Job Duty Facilities and Resources: Ensure that facilities, laboratories, and equipment meet the educational needs of students and faculty Job Duty Accreditation and Compliance: Ensure compliance with accreditation standards and regulations set forth by dental boards and accrediting bodies Job Duty Community Engagement: Represent the dental school within the larger university community and engage with external stakeholders, including alumni, donors, and industry partners Job Duty Advocacy: Advocate for the dental school s interests at local, state, and national levels, influencing policy and promoting the value of dental education and research Job Duty Research Support: Encourage and support faculty research initiatives, promoting a culture of scholarly inquiry and innovation within the dental school Job Duty Technology Integration: Explore and integrate new technologies and methodologies into dental education and practice to enhance learning outcomes and clinical training Job Duty Strategic Vision: Develop and implement strategic plans to advance the mission and goals of the dental school, ensuring long-term sustainability and growth Job Duty Fundraising: Collaborate with development officers to secure funding through grants, donations, and partnerships to support research, facilities, and student scholarships Job Duty Perform additional responsibilities as required to support the mission, goals, and needs of the department and institution Posting Detail Information Posting Number S05340P Job Open Date 06/02/2026 Job Close Date 04/30/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/44838 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk