    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/46114": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Clinical Dentistry Faculty",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor Clinical Dentistry Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Assistant Professor Clinical Dentistry Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor Clinical Dentistry Faculty Department Dental Clinic Position Category Faculty Job Description The Lincoln Memorial University-College of Dental Medicine ( LMU - CDM ) is seeking Clinical General Dentistry Faculty at the LMU -Tower and LMU Community Care Clinics. The position reports to the Dean for Clinical Affairs and is responsible for supervising LMU - CDM students in the Centers for Excellence (CE) to provide care to their patient family Required Qualifications D.D.S. or D.M.D. degree Must have knowledge of dental practice operation Must be highly skilled in general dentistry Adaptable and motivated Able to work independently Team oriented Personable Qualifications Skills Required Experience in private practice where dentistry is performed. Experience in a dental teaching environment is preferred Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Campus LMU Tower Job Duty Job Duty Supervise students in the comprehensive care unit to provide comprehensive care to their patient family Job Duty Maintain Standards of Care and ensure continuity of care for all patients in the Centers for Excellence Job Duty Participate in clinic quality assurance and continuous quality improvement measures Job Duty Work on the clinic floor 5 days per week, depending on faculty practice day Job Duty Assist the staff, faculty, and administration in Knoxville to train the adjunct faculty to achieve clinical calibration Job Duty Work with the dental assistant(s) and Clinic Care Coordinator and contribute to performance review evaluations in conjunction with the Dean for Clinical Affairs and Associate Dean for Clinical Affairs Job Duty Coordinate with the Associate Dean for Faculty and Students for staff leave (vacation, medical) and clinic floor coverage Job Duty Complete administrative reports as needed and all LMU -required employee training Job Duty Track student progress and collaborate with Center for Excellence Attending Faculty and the Dean Clinical Affairs and Associate Dean for Clinical Affairs on student deficiencies Job Duty Assure patient, students, and staff safety and communication Job Duty Perform dental procedures on patients as needed Job Duty Serve on committees as assigned Job Duty Support/participate in an after-hours emergency care program as needed Job Duty Perform additional duties as assigned by the Dean for Clinical Affairs Posting Detail Information Posting Number F01550P Job Open Date 07/29/2025 Job Close Date 12/31/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks