      "title": "Part-Time Assistant Professor of Dental Medicine",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Part-Time Assistant Professor of Dental Medicine Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Part-Time Assistant Professor of Dental Medicine Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Part-Time Assistant Professor of Dental Medicine Department College of Dental Medicine Position Category Faculty Part Time Job Description The General Dentistry and Specialty Faculty in the College of Dental Medicine is responsible for teaching all forms of comprehensive general dentistry to pre-doctoral students. The General Dentistry and Specialty Faculty reports directly to the Vice Dean for Academic and Clinical Education and works in close cooperation with the Office of the Dean to support the Schools programs and initiatives Required Qualifications . DDS or DMD from a Commission on Dental Accreditation ( CODA ) accredited institution . Minimum of 15 years of private practice experience . 5 years teaching experience . AEGD , GPR , or Specialty training preferred . Forensic Fellowship Certification preferred . Eligibility for dental licensure in Tennessee Full time or Part time: Full and/or Part Time Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Campus LMU Tower Job Duty Job Duty . Instructing pre-doctoral students in the following environments: simulation laboratory, didactic (classroom / seminar), and clinic. Job Duty . Willingness to learn or apply the skills to prepare and teach pre-clinical General Dentistry Job Duty . Willingness and ability to cover pre-doctoral students in the clinical setting in procedures as pertaining to the General Dentistry Clinic Model of the College of Dental Medicine. Job Duty . Helping ensure that the dental 