    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45274": {
      "title": "Didactic Staff Assistant",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Didactic Staff Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Didactic Staff Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Didactic Staff Assistant Department Physician Assistant Program Chattanooga Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Didactic Education Assistant is a key member of the Physician Assistant (PA) Programs administrative team Required Qualifications Experience working in healthcare education, education, or research environment. Familiarity with statitistical analysis or research Strong organizational, technical, and communication skills. Associate or bachelors degree in public health, statistics, or related field. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Campus Chattanooga Job Duty Job Duty Provide administrative support to the Didactic Director of Education and didactic faculty in the implementation and management of the PA program didactic curriculum Job Duty Assist with the coordination and organization of didactic courses and instructional activities, including scheduling, classroom preparation, and distribution of course materials Job Duty Support the management of course documentation, including syllabi, learning objectives, lecture materials, and course resources within the program s learning management system Job Duty Assist faculty with exam preparation, formatting, distribution, and secure storage of assessments Job Duty Provide administrative assistance for course evaluations, exam reviews, and other instructional activities Job Duty Maintain organized records of didactic curriculum materials, assessment documents, and program evaluation data Job Duty Assist with coordination of faculty meetings, curriculum meetings, and accreditation-related activities, including preparation of meeting materials and documentation of minutes Job Duty Support communication with students, faculty, and university departments regarding didactic curriculum activities and scheduling Job Duty Assist with maintaining educational technology and classroom resources used in didactic instruction Job Duty Provide primary administrative support for the Director of Assessment for continuous quality improvement activities Job Duty Assist with collection, organization, and tracking of program evaluation data, including course evaluations, exam performance data, and student feedback Job Duty Support the preparation of assessment reports and data summaries used for internal program review and accreditation reporting Job Duty Maintain organized documentation related to the program s self-assessment plan and ARC -PA accreditation requirements Job Duty Assist faculty and program leadership with data entry, record maintenance, and documentation needed for accreditation evidence and program review Job Duty Track completion of faculty assessment activities, course reviews, and curriculum improvement initiatives Job Duty Provide administrative support for faculty research and scholarly activities Job Duty Assist with literature searches, formatting manuscripts, preparing presentation materials, and organizing research documentation as directed by faculty Job Duty Support coordination of research meetings, project timelines, and documentation of scholarly work Job Duty Assist faculty with tracking publications, presentations, and scholarly output for program reporting Job Duty Provide administrative assistance related to institutional research compliance processes, when applicable Job Duty Provide day-to-day administrative support to didactic faculty, including assistance with scheduling meetings, coordinating course activities, and managing instructional materials Job Duty Assist with coordination of student academic activities, including review sessions, course communications, and distribution of instructional resources Job Duty Respond to routine inquiries from students and faculty regarding didactic curriculum logistics and scheduling Job Duty Assist faculty with course organization and administrative tasks to support efficient delivery of instruction Job Duty Support program faculty and leadership in program events, meetings, and academic activities Job Duty Assist with preparation and coordination of program retreats, faculty development sessions, and accreditation-related events Job Duty Participate in program and university activities as assigned Job Duty Perform other duties as assigned in support of the PA program mission and the University mission Posting Detail Information Posting Number S05314P Job Open Date 05/19/2026 Job Close Date 09/19/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor v