    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45921": {
      "title": "Life Support Skills Training Coordinator",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Life Support Skills Training Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Life Support Skills Training Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Life Support Skills Training Coordinator Department AHA Training Center Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Life Support Skills Coordinator, located at the Brandon Fl campus, executes regional delivery, instructor allocation, and skills verification for American Heart Association ( AHA ) courses across their designated geographic campus cluster. This role ensures that student certifications are processed swiftly and compliant with all emergency cardiovascular care guidelines. This role reports directly to the Director of Life Support Skills Education Required Qualifications Valid AHA BLS / ACLS / PALS Instructor credentials required (Qualified Individual). Preferred Qualifications 2+ years of active experience teaching life support skills Physical Demands Campus Brandon Florida Job Duty Job Duty Course Execution: Lead regional BLS , ACLS , and PALS training courses and conduct high-stakes on-site physical skills checks Job Duty Local Administration: Set regional class schedules in coordination with the Director and program partners, manage regional course rosters, and process e-card request paperwork Job Duty Remediation Management: Deliver direct, structured student remediation for individuals struggling to meet passing criteria during cognitive or hands-on testing Job Duty Inventory Control: Provide on-site maintenance, cleaning, and tracking for resuscitation manikins, feedback devices, and local training site supplies Job Duty Instructor Coordination: Assist in certifying, assigning and monitoring program clinical faculty and if needed local adjunct AHA instructors scheduled to support large training cohorts Job Duty Professional Development & Knowledge Sharing: Attend at least one national or regional conference per year related to core responsibilities to bring back innovative practices and knowledge to faculty and staff. Support and/or hold airway training skills sessions upon request Job Duty Multi-Site Mobility: Travel between university locations and regional campuses as needed to meet the operational requirements of the job Job Duty Key Competencies Instructional excellence in clinical resuscitations. Clear communication and remediation patience. Strict adherence to standardized testing criteria Job Duty Zero compliance infractions or processing delays regarding local rosters, attendance validation, and swift remote e-card distribution Job Duty 100% passing rates of required certifications achieved through patient, highly effective, and structured local remediation frameworks for struggling students Job Duty Pristine upkeep, sanitary compliance, and detailed tracking of localized resuscitation manikins, feedback devices, and safety gear Job Duty Seamless allocation and rigorous monitoring of local adjunct AHA instructors to ensure uniform, high-quality instructional delivery during large group cohorts Posting Detail Information Posting Number S05454P Job Open Date 08/25/2026 Job Close Date 12/25/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education 