    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/46015": {
      "title": "Accreditation and Integration Coordinator for Health Science, Knoxville",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Accreditation and Integration Coordinator for Health Science, Knoxville Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Accreditation and Integration Coordinator for Health Science, Knoxville Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Accreditation and Integration Coordinator for Health Science, Knoxville Department Health Sciences Simulations Position Category Staff Full Time Job Description The Accreditation and Integration Coordinator for Health Sciences provides high-level executive administrative, analytical, and logistical support directly to the Chief Accreditation and Integration Officer ( CAIO ). This role serves as a centralized administrative anchor specifically focused on supporting the accreditation processes and the operational workflows of the Center for IPE and Simulation ( CIPES ). Operating within a unified enterprise structure, this position supports the CAIO’s direct reports within Simulation Operations, Simulation and SP Programming, Interprofessional Education ( IPE ), and Life Support Skills. This role reports directly to the Chief Accreditation and Integration Officer for Health Sciences Required Qualifications Associate degree required Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in business administration, healthcare administration, education, or a related field preferred 3+ years of experience in a high-level administrative support, executive assistant, or program coordination role. Demonstrated experience working within a complex higher education, health professions program, or academic healthcare environment strongly preferred Physical Demands Campus Lmu- West Knoxville Job Duty Job Duty Document Control and Review: Assist the CAIO with the clerical formatting, systematic organization, and digital archiving of all required accreditation documents across multiple health professions programs to ensure consistency, timeliness, and completeness prior to submission Job Duty Standards Tracking: Maintain highly organized master repositories of current and future accreditation standards across multiple health professions colleges (including LMU - DCOM ) to support multi-program alignment Job Duty Audit Readiness: Monitor compliance communications and timeline trackers to ensure all multi-site program metrics are finalized ahead of cyclical reporting deadlines or internal audits Job Duty Direct Report Support: Provide direct administrative support to CIPES leadership, managing travel requests, processing institutional expense reports, and coordinating multi-site calendars for the CAIO’s direct reports to eliminate operational silos Job Duty Office Operations: Handle comprehensive clerical duties for the CAIO executive suite and CIPES , including processing receipts, routing document approvals, managing multi-campus correspondence, and maintaining central files Job Duty Executive & Committee Assistance: Coordinate high-level leadership and committee meetings, distribute strategic agendas, and record detailed minutes to prevent cross-program scheduling conflicts Job Duty KPI Data Collection: Systematically collect, clean, and organize raw operational data, validation metrics, and key performance indicators (KPIs) across Simulation, IPE , and Life Support Skills Job Duty Database & Roster Management: Maintain comprehensive and highly accurate records, including student cohort assignments, certification histories, cross-program group setups, and active campus personnel rosters Job Duty Resource & Budget Tracking: Organize and report on daily CIPES operations to give leadership clear visibility into how staff, spaces, and equipment are used, efficiently driving and supporting better budget management Job Duty Unified Support: Promote a unified “one LMU ” culture by streamlining communication and standardizing administrative workflows across all CIPES activities and health professions campuses Job Duty High proficiency in database management, Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, Teams), and enterprise scheduling/expense software Job Duty Meticulous attention to detail and exceptional organizational skills required for managing complex accreditation portfolios Job Duty Data-driven analytical skills to aggregate raw metrics into clean, actionable data reports Job Duty Operational discipline and efficiency, with the ability to manage requests from multiple direct reports simultaneously while keeping strategic priorities aligned Job Duty High confidentiality and professionalism in dealing with institutional records, financial data, and multi-program accreditation files Job Duty Continuous Accreditation Success: 100% accuracy and completeness in the clerical formatting, organization, and secure digital archiving of compliance and program metrics, ensuring all submissions are delivered ahead of internal reviews and external deadlines for multiple health professions programs Job Duty CIPES Operational & Margin Efficiency: Flawless, timely administrative execution of travel requests, expense reports, and logistics for all direct reports, successfully eliminating multi-site administrative delays and tracking resource expenditures to drive margin improvement Job Duty Flawless Data Integrity: Maintenance of completely accurate centralized student tracking cohorts, evaluation statistics, and performance KPIs across CIPES to provide clear, reliable operational visibility Job Duty Elimination of Operational Silos: Highly coordinated calendar and shared timeline management that facilitates cross-campus collaboration and supports the alignment of all health professions simulation and IPE spaces under a unified LMU framework. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S05458P Job Open Date 08/26/2026 Job Close Date 11/26/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45832 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts Curriculum Vitae To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/44758": {
      "title": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Principal Faculty, PA Program Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Principal Faculty, PA Program Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Principal Faculty, PA Program Department PA Program Harrogate Position Category Faculty Job Description The Physician Assistant Program clinical faculty shall have the responsibility of developing, executing, and monitoring clinical sites and preceptors, assuring compliance with SACS , ARCPA , and SMS policies and standards. The clinical faculty shall create and/or edit rotation-specific syllabi and preceptor evaluations of students. The clinical faculty shall be involved in teaching, evaluation and assessment, advisement, mentoring, and student compliance with LMU SMS policies. The clinical faculty shall participate in the recruitment, admissions and selection process, and program organization, evaluation, planning, administration, and management, and assist in continuous review and analysis of the LMU PA program curriculum effectiveness in preparation for program assessment by SACS , ARCPA , and SMS . Required Qualifications Graduation from an accredited physician assistant training program and certification by NCCPA ; current licensure or eligibility for Tennessee licensure; *possession of a masters degree in physician assistant studies and actively engaged or willing to obtain a doctoral degree in a field related to medical science; *minimum of two years full-time clinical experience as a physician assistant; *excellent oral, written, organizational, and computer skills. Preferred Qualifications *Doctoral degree in a field related to medical science or education; *teaching experience in classroom and clinical settings, preferably in an institution of higher learning; *program administrative or leadership experience; *evidence of potential for excellence in teaching and scholarly activity. Physical Demands Campus Harrogate Job Duty Job Duty Promote the mission of Lincoln Memorial University to all faculty, staff, students, and to the community at large; Job Duty Promote effective working relationships among faculty, staff, and students; Job Duty Responsible for working with the Director of Clinical Education to identify and develop new clinical sites for PA clinical rotations and perform clinical site visits Job Duty Oversee qualitative and quantitative evaluations of students Job Duty Involved in program organization, evaluation, planning, administration and management as well as assist in continuous review and analysis of the program s effectiveness and preparation for program assessment by ARC -PA, LMU , SACSCOC , and others Job Duty Provide teaching, evaluation, advisement and mentoring of PA students Job Duty Work with LMU - SMS faculty and staff on an ongoing basis to maintain program compliance with the Accreditation Review Commission on Education for the Physician Assistant ( ARC -PA) and the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools ( SACS ) criteria for accreditation and reaccreditation; Job Duty Fulfill the University s scholarship expectation through research, publication, grant development, creative achievement, and other endeavors consistent with the Faculty/Staff Policy Manual; Job Duty Provide committee service and attend SMS , PA program and LMU faculty meetings Job Duty Develop course schedules, syllabi and student evaluation mechanisms; Job Duty Serve as Course Director for Clinical Phase courses as assigned and complete End-of-Course reports for assigned Clinical Phase courses and present conclusions based on data analysis and recommendations for action(s)/modification(s) to the Curriculum Committee. Job Duty Design, implement, coordinate, and evaluate learning and assessment activities for EOS days. Job Duty Assist in revising the Student Handbook and the Student Catalog as assigned. Job Duty Participate in the Program s continuous self-assessment process as directed. Job Duty Assist in recruiting, developing, evaluating, and maintaining clinical sites and clinical preceptors for Clinical Phase Supervised Clinical Practice Experiences (SCPEs). Job Duty Revise the Clinical Site/Preceptor Handbook with the assistance of the DCE and Clinical Site and Rotations Manager. Job Duty Develop, evaluate, and revise policies and procedures for the Clinical Phase with the DCE . Job Duty Participate in PA student selection; Job Duty Assure the availability of remedial instruction, as needed and assigned; Job Duty Participate in the design, implementation, coordination, and evaluation of PA program curriculum; Job Duty assist in the administration and evaluation of the PA program; Job Duty Assist in the search process for selecting PA program faculty; Job Duty establish a personal program of scholarly activity; Job Duty Write, edit, review, and approve learning objectives and test items; Job Duty Secure, orient, and evaluate clinical preceptors Job Duty Provide feedback to instructors/preceptors to help them improve teaching skills; Job Duty Monitor student progress; serve as primary academic advisor for clinical year students; Job Duty Perform service activities that advance the PA program, SMS , and the PA profession, including assistance in the recruitment, orientation, and retention of PA students; as assigned; Job Duty Exhibit/recruit at various meetings as needed; *fulfill faculty responsibilities as outlined in the Faculty/Staff Policy Manual; Job Duty Complete required institutional, program accreditation, and other reports necessary for the advancement of University programs, both on campus and at extended campus sites; Job Duty and perform other duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F01758P Job Open Date 05/29/2026 Job Close Date 09/29/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/44757 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/46155": {
      "title": "Instructor of Nursing",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Instructor of Nursing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Instructor of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Instructor of Nursing Department ASN Nursing Program Position Category Faculty Job Description The instructional faculty member shall have the primary responsibility of the teaching function and shall be held accountable for the teaching obligations as it contributes to the attainment of the mission of the University, the School, and the Department Required Qualifications A minimum of a masters degree in nursing required for all CSON Faculty positions; a doctorate is required for teaching in the CSON graduate programs, doctorate in Nursing recommended; current unrestricted Tennessee licensure and licensure in other states if required for teaching/clinical supervision; and evidence of potential for effective teaching and scholarly activity. Applicant should demonstrate effective communication skills; and sufficient mastery of assigned discipline Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Campus Cedar Bluff Job Duty Job Duty Promote the mission of Lincoln Memorial University to all faculty, staff, students and to the community at large: undertake the Standard Instructional/Research/Service Workload as outlined in the Faculty-Staff Policy Manual Job Duty provide course and classroom conduct as outlined in the Faculty-Staff Policy Manual Job Duty provide academic advisement of students Job Duty conduct office/conference hours Job Duty submit textbook requests Job Duty comply with announced requirements Job Duty engage in professional development Job Duty provide committee service Job Duty attend faculty meetings Job Duty attend commencement activities Job Duty participate in annual faculty evaluation Job Duty completion of required institutional and program accreditation reports and other reports necessary for the operation and advancement of the University Job Duty and perform other duties as assigned. Job Duty precept graduate students in a clinical or non-clinical setting Posting Detail Information Posting Number F01846P Job Open Date 09/25/2026 Job Close Date 03/25/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/46152 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
