    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/46159": {
      "title": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Teacher Field Supervisor, Graduate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Teacher Field Supervisor, Graduate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Teacher Field Supervisor, Graduate Department M. Ed. Position Category Staff Part Time Job Description The Student Teacher Field Supervisor reports to the Program Director or Chair of the program, and Dean of the Carter & Moyers School of Education. This person will work closely with students and designated faculty and assist with the supervision of field-based and clinical activities for Student Teachers in local area schools Required Qualifications A minimum of a masters degree in education. Relevant experience and appropriate credentials/licensure and/or demonstrated competence in teaching; good professional standing Preferred Qualifications Doctoral Degree in Education from an accredited institution of higher education Physical Demands Prior experience supervising, mentoring, coaching, or evaluating teachers or teacher candidates in K-12 school settings. Administrative experience and/or evaluative experience using the Tennessee Educator Acceleration Model ( TEAM ). Campus Remote Job Duty Job Duty promote the mission of Lincoln Memorial University to all faculty, staff, students and to the community at large Job Duty promote effective working relationships among faculty, staff and students Job Duty assist the designated faculty with field-based experiences for students in an efficient, professional, and supportive manner; work closely with cooperating teachers as the candidate learns the student teaching process and acquires the knowledge, understanding, and the entry-level skills required in the teaching discipline Job Duty maintain records and evaluations as requested, for activities the students complete during the field-based experiences Job Duty complete required institutional, program accreditation and other reports as requested Job Duty works closely with both student teachers and job-embedded candidates in K-12 field placements Job Duty travel to partner district schools and assigned field placement sites are required Job Duty perform other duties as assigned Posting Detail Information Posting Number S05342P Job Open Date 09/04/2026 Job Close Date 12/31/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/44865 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required